  "question": {
    "text": "A $6.0$ volt battery is connected to two light bulbs as shown in figure. Light bulb 1 has resistance 3 ohm while light bulb 2 has resistance $6 \\mathrm{ohm}$. Battery has negligible internal resistance. Which bulb will glow brighter?\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/OF5bumPGCZwfxKPvceusVYiurs7-JoePpoD8K30Kh-4.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NQIjH",
      "text": "\nBulb 1 will glow more first and then its brightness will become less than bulb 2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "W7g9s",
      "text": "\nBulb 1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "h5aFN",
      "text": "\nBulb 2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eMsZW",
      "text": "\nBoth glow equally",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Total resistance $=\\frac{6 \\times 3}{6+3}=2 \\Omega$ Current in circuit $=\\frac{6}{2}=3 A$\nTherefore current through bulb 1 is $2 \\mathrm{~A}$ and bulb 2 is $1 A$. So bulb 1 will glow more.",
    "image": null
  },
